From bfbaf6296c4c60e825f316c89b20f97c3b0a23c5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Philippe Simons <simons.philippe@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 17:24:48 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] feat(Input): focus profile instead of InputPlumber's
 intercept mode

OpenGamepadUI no longer sets an intercept mode. While it has focus every
gamepad gets assets/gamepad/profiles/ogui_focus.json, which sends each
input to DBus as the UI action the intercept used to produce and lets
none reach the game. While a game has focus, its profile is loaded, in
priority order: the game's own profile from the settings, a profile the
launcher declared in $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/opengamepadui/game_profile (path,
then the owning pid), the global profile.

The game's profile now carries what the intercept did for Guide: a JSON
profile that does not map Guide gets Guide -> [layer, ui_guide], and the
layer Guide holds gets OpenGamepadUI's combos where the profile leaves
them free (Guide+South -> ui_quick, the quick bar; Guide+North ->
ui_osk). With InputPlumber's deferred activation outputs, a lone Guide
tap opens the main menu and a combo does not. The JSON is edited
directly, after the target modification, because InputPlumberProfile
drops `layers` (save_target_modified_profile split out for that).

A combo that opens a menu while Guide is held loads the focus profile,
so the Guide release can arrive without its press; it is ignored
instead of opening the main menu over the quick bar.

The single-capability intercept flipped to Always on the Guide press,
so a profile's input layer (Guide held + R1) never reached the game.

Also fixes set_gamepad_profile(): it broke out of the device loop as
soon as a device had a gamepad target, before loading anything.
